# The process kits — the method layer.
#
# Ignored by default, deliberately and reversibly. They are portable copies of
# the five-phase process, not this project's code, and publishing the method is
# a separate decision from publishing the product. Delete these five lines to
# make it, and it becomes part of what the repository argues.
#
# `docs/product/` stays tracked either way — the OUTPUT of the process is the
# evidence, and that is the half a reader actually needs.
/discovery-kit/
/design-kit/
/develop-kit/
/deploy-kit/
/release-kit/

# Secrets. This repository is public from its first commit; nothing here is a
# key, and the deployed demo is intended to need none.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Toolchain output — the stack is not chosen yet (cycle 0 decides it), so this
# covers the likely candidates rather than pretending to know.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Foundry, from cycle 5 onward
/cache/
/broadcast/
/lib/forge-std/

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
